  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1833b97b4e8284e489c3555d5dace838, type: 3}
  m_Name: HZ_PY_06_FUNCTIONS
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: HZ_PY_06_FUNCTIONS
  language: 1
  topic: Functions
  difficulty: 1
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Type the missing keyword so the function sends the code back to print.
  code: "def get_code():\n    ____ code\n\nprint(get_code())"
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: return
  runTests:
  - setup: code = 4321
    expectedOutput: 4321
  - setup: code = 7
    expectedOutput: 7
  explanation: return sends a value back to the place that called the function, so
    print(get_code()) prints 4321.
  hint: It's the keyword that hands a value back from a function.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: That keyword doesn't send a value back. print only shows a
    value - the function needs the keyword that hands a value back to the code that
    called it.
